would_approve:
A 10-year Solo fps, our preferred ramp, in a grid that supports it. On this grid the 10-year at Renton:
- passes Rating first (S3 -1.75, $1.08B clear);
- passes Downside (worst column -0.92);
- passes Fundable ($0.0B stress peak);
- passes One development at a time (when alone);
- fails Business case by $1.86B (-0.86 against the +$1B bar).
So we would not approve it this round.

The 10-year is the right ramp. Alone it is within ε of the 7-year in every column (+0.87 to +0.93), so the smaller bill wins ($60.32B against $65.00B). With the Re-engine it leads by $1.00-1.06B and has the higher worst column (-2.53 at Renton against -3.53).

