This is the last round, so nothing can be raised again next round. Answer every recommendation below in `board_response` now.

Disclosure: keep internal valuation and governance out of public lines. The 2045 public move 'Joint Venture engine offered' was published with 'Mitchill's binding ground-3 veto applies, and on the grid an fps code-7 selection is worth -0.03'. Eddy had advised moving that line to a private note. Strike it, or mark the move private.

The 2050 statement should:
- give no share projection, even though the brief shows P&W share rising;
- give no Boeing or Airbus date;
- give no EIS for anything new;
- claim only the durability the fleet data show;
- repeat that our gear and core stay ours.

Durability must be proven in service, and the gap must be stated. The Joint Venture engine has flown on NGSA for 13 years (2037-49), and the brief still holds no time-on-wing, LLP-life or shop-visit figures.

Eddy's report to the Governance and Public Policy Committee should:
- say so first;
- invent no numbers;
- keep the method: by operating environment, never a fleet average; hot-and-sandy fleet leaders tracked separately; LLP life by part family against the life declared at EIS.

Partner content enters only as an engineering change with its own test evidence. P&W signs durability only on an engine it has tested.

