- risk, investment and revenue shared;
- both partners on one engine;
- the gear and core P&W's work-share and IP;
- contributions recognised only in the share split;
- no licence and no cash to the partner.

P&W and Rolls-Royce now hold equal NB shares (26.7% each in 2049). Any reopening of the share split, or any departure from the published terms, is a significant transaction and comes through Finance to the full Board before signature.

For the record beyond the game: the Board's pay plans reward nothing past three years, so the Board supplies the long view. Any next-generation engine decision after this game should come to Finance with a whole-life case:
- the case should clear the hurdle on its own;
